Read //Patterns of Enterprise Application Architecture// by Martin Fowler a bit. The patterns, yes. A very fun read it was, until the initial chapters ended, and the patterns themselves started. Wow, that's unreadable on my phone! Will get to it later.

Then I moved on to the O. G. patterns book, //A Pattern Language// by many an author, the heavy paper copy gifted by [[Flancian]] (thank you!), including his annotations. Read through a third.

Read some manga. Finished my nth re-reading of Girls' Last Tour, re-read a few volumes of Mushishi. Both in limited paper Russian edition. I'm a big fan. Also reading Tower Dungeon by Tsutomu Nihei in ongoing.

For university, been reading Klaus Schwab's //The Fourth Industrial Revolution// in Russian translation. Maybe it's the translation, but it's such a bad book, both in art value and economic knowledge. Got a few chapters left.

For a few months, been re-reading [[The Glass Bead Game]] in English translation.

Since June, been reading The Dispossessed.